<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:07:35Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Decolonizing perceptions about Africa</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:72c7fddffe343bb5d33f769dd344a391c15c83d3130fa243023c1b2be256c4f8</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:07:23Z</updated><published>2026-09-20T06:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/decolonizing-perceptions-about-africa/a-79331178--8deea6e78a06.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/decolonizing-perceptions-about-africa/a-79331178?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As a UN resolution alters the standard global map to reflect the continent more accurately, initiatives to decolonize African schools and a campaign to present positive developments are changing the way Africa is seen.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine steps up measures to protect railways</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f75663238db7c8f1797f47a753f24834dd8153f412372c8d130c294416df838</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T15:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-steps-up-measures-to-protect-railways/a-79339087--356ca60a409d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-steps-up-measures-to-protect-railways/a-79339087?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Russia increases its attacks on Ukraine's rail infrastructure, the Ukrainian government has called for help to replace destroyed locomotives and is making plans to keep passengers safe.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ever more Israelis moving to and investing in Cyprus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b96632efcbb9ccc1667d02f4bf56299c950938d6b5637f761a291d54fe31d527</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T06:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ever-more-israelis-moving-to-and-investing-in-cyprus/a-79330240--f9d83a8ed500.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ever-more-israelis-moving-to-and-investing-in-cyprus/a-79330240?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Over the past three years, more and more Israelis have been purchasing property and investing in Cyprus, with many moving to the island permanently. How has this changed the Cypriot economy and how are locals responding?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Yemeni militants: How powerful are the Houthis now?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9b413aa89ee49a7d3bf3ec1a3c230e0e7885a4c23ee38bdbd90f3fd7723c12ce</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:07:35Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T19:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemeni-militants-how-powerful-are-the-houthis-now/a-79331945--7be9859826c2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemeni-militants-how-powerful-are-the-houthis-now/a-79331945?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After Houthi victories in Yemen, the group's importance in the US-Iran war has grown. Previously Lebanon's Hezbollah was considered most significant in Iran's "axis of resistance." Now the Houthis are rising to the top.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Airport malaria in Germany remains infrequent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:804add3025d923a2c653278c6f4f6414168c261f9eda0ccb2a5c4cf19fe4f5f1</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T18:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/airport-malaria-in-germany-remains-infrequent/a-79333920--b6e9f1b4961f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/airport-malaria-in-germany-remains-infrequent/a-79333920?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An outbreak of malaria at Frankfurt Airport this summer has raised alarm. Experts believe parasites probably arrived in a passenger's luggage. But with the onset of fall, the risks of contracting the disease are low.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Canada and EU: A look at the bloc's special relationships</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cab85cdb0c5701290814075a545ccbd028538d979bcbee70f6ee5bcbdaef58ef</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T14:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-and-eu-a-look-at-the-bloc-s-special-relationships/a-79328797--41616c65f5bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-and-eu-a-look-at-the-bloc-s-special-relationships/a-79328797?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Though Canada may be some distance from Europe geographically, closer political ties are in the cards. With talk of an associate membership, DW takes a look at other arrangements the EU has with particular countries.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>High-profile raids spotlight India's food-safety struggles</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85a6f0a495b17f6569f7796141adf8e9eb8b7a7828d7edf321eb67f0775837fb</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/high-profile-raids-spotlight-india-s-food-safety-struggles/a-79324342--7a2317b19494.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/high-profile-raids-spotlight-india-s-food-safety-struggles/a-79324342?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Recent raids at luxury hotels and a wider crackdown on food companies have renewed the debate about food-safety standards and enforcement in India.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Aztec manuscript returns to Mexico after two centuries, on loan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd5716672b6621e622b08a26264b05d664fc616f625f4791b5380123310ff10b</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T03:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/aztec-manuscript-returns-to-mexico-after-two-centuries-on-loan/a-79316983--e03b036933bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/aztec-manuscript-returns-to-mexico-after-two-centuries-on-loan/a-79316983?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For years, Mexico has demanded the return of a treasured manuscript. Now the Aztec relic is back home from France — but on loan.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russian birth tourism to Brazil increases</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a279f3746e0e03a53baafa690b27dcf8240655d79239963ab2c573a6b5909073</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T19:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-birth-tourism-to-brazil-increases/a-79312304--01a0fcbb92e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-birth-tourism-to-brazil-increases/a-79312304?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine and stricter regulations in Argentina, more and more Russians are choosing to travel to Brazil to give birth to children, who will obtain Brazilian nationality.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>A war-fatigued and anxious Russia picks a new parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ecce66e2ae4d6331f746c8912c28dbf05ebe400b5bc5b145aadec34853cb4f5</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T16:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-war-fatigued-and-anxious-russia-picks-a-new-parliament/a-79312440--1588122e0cc9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-war-fatigued-and-anxious-russia-picks-a-new-parliament/a-79312440?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fuel shortages, drone strikes and mobilization rumors are fueling anxiety and war fatigue in Russia. As support for peace talks grows among Russians, the Kremlin is watching closely ahead of parliamentary elections.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Smuggling suspected as more rare animals seen in India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f7904d7edc46966f02cb02afc62656b7fe4676ea30e8012c66e1025d4eb0c5b</id><updated>2026-09-20T13:06:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/smuggling-suspected-as-more-rare-animals-seen-in-india/a-79309352--d0621e7dbde3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/smuggling-suspected-as-more-rare-animals-seen-in-india/a-79309352?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Orangutans, rare reptiles and other exotic animals are popping up in India, suggesting the country is becoming a major destination for trafficked wildlife.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
